## 6. Conversation Memory: `conversation_mem_available` Parsing Robustness

**Component:** `include/strata/core/conversation_memory.hpp` / `src/core/conversation_memory.cpp`

**Responsibilities:** Parses `/proc/meminfo`'s `MemAvailable` line to decide whether parking a conversation snapshot is safe.

**Problem:** The function signature takes `std::istream&`, but the implementation (not shown, but implied by the header) likely does a substring search for `"MemAvailable:"`. On some kernels the line has trailing whitespace or the value is followed by `" kB"` with variable spacing. A `std::stoull` on a substring that includes `" kB"` throws.

**Proposed change:** Parse with `std::istringstream` line-by-line, extracting the numeric field by position rather than by substring offset.

```diff
--- a/include/strata/core/conversation_memory.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/core/conversation_memory.hpp
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@
 namespace strata::core {

 std::optional<uint64_t> conversation_available_memory();
-std::optional<uint64_t> conversation_mem_available(std::istream& meminfo);
+std::optional<uint64_t> conversation_mem_available(std::istream& meminfo);  // parses "MemAvailable:  N kB"

 inline bool conversation_memory_admit(std::optional<uint64_t> available,
                                       uint64_t allocation, uint64_t floor) {
```

The actual fix is in the `.cpp`:

```diff
--- a/src/core/conversation_memory.cpp
+++ b/src/core/conversation_memory.cpp
@@ -12,10 +12,12 @@
 std::optional<uint64_t> conversation_mem_available(std::istream& meminfo) {
     std::string line;
     while (std::getline(meminfo, line)) {
-        if (line.rfind("MemAvailable:", 0) == 0) {
-            const auto pos = line.find_first_of("0123456789");
-            if (pos != std::string::npos)
-                return std::stoull(line.substr(pos)) * 1024;
+        if (line.rfind("MemAvailable:", 0) == 0) {
+            std::istringstream ss(line.substr(13));
+            uint64_t kb = 0;
+            std::string unit;
+            if (ss >> kb && (unit.empty() || unit == "kB"))
+                return kb * 1024;
         }
     }
     return std::nullopt;
```

**Verification cases:**
1. Input `"MemAvailable:   12345 kB\n"` returns `12345 * 1024`.
2. Input `"MemAvailable:\n"` (malformed, no number) returns `std::nullopt` without throwing.

