## 2. GGUF Split Path Resolution: Symlink and Case Sensitivity

**Component:** `include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp` — `gguf_split_paths()`

**Responsibility:** Resolves any shard path to the full ordered list of shard files for a split model.

**Problem:** The function uses `std::ifstream(p, std::ios::binary)` to test existence. On Windows with Hugging Face snapshot symlinks (junction points), `ifstream` may succeed on the symlink target but the resolved path may differ from what the engine later opens. Additionally, the five-digit format check `any.size() != at + 4 + 5 + 5` is fragile: a path with a trailing space or a `.gguf` extension in uppercase (`.GGUF`) fails silently and returns a single-element vector, causing the engine to open only one shard.

**Proposed change:** Normalize the extension comparison to be case-insensitive, and use `std::filesystem::exists` (C++17) instead of `ifstream` for the existence probe.

```diff
--- a/include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp
@@ -#include <cstdio>
 #include <fstream>
 #include <stdexcept>
 #include <string>
 #include <vector>
+#include <filesystem>
+#include <algorithm>
+#include <cctype>

 namespace strata {

+inline bool ends_with_ci(const std::string& s, const std::string& suffix) {
+    if (s.size() < suffix.size()) return false;
+    for (size_t i = 0; i < suffix.size(); ++i)
+        if (std::tolower((unsigned char)s[s.size() - suffix.size() + i]) !=
+            std::tolower((unsigned char)suffix[i]))
+            return false;
+    return true;
+}
+
 inline std::vector<std::string> gguf_split_paths(const std::string& any) {
     static const char tag[] = "-of-";
     const size_t at = any.rfind(tag);
-    // "...-NNNNN-of-MMMMM.gguf": five digits before the tag, five after it, then the extension
-    if (at == std::string::npos || at < 6 || any[at - 6] != '-' || any.size() != at + 4 + 5 + 5 ||
-        any.compare(at + 9, 5, ".gguf") != 0)
+    // "...-NNNNN-of-MMMMM.gguf": five digits before the tag, five after it, then the extension (case-insensitive)
+    if (at == std::string::npos || at < 6 || any[at - 6] != '-' ||
+        any.size() < at + 4 + 5 + 5 || !ends_with_ci(any, ".gguf"))
         return {any};
+    // verify the five digits after the tag are actually digits
+    for (size_t i = 0; i < 5; ++i) {
+        const char c = any[at + 4 + i];
+        if (c < '0' || c > '9') return {any};
+    }
     int no = 0, n = 0;
     for (size_t i = 0; i < 5; ++i) {
         const char a = any[at - 5 + i], b = any[at + 4 + i];
         if (a < '0' || a > '9' || b < '0' || b > '9') return {any};
         no = no * 10 + (a - '0');
         n = n * 10 + (b - '0');
     }
     if (n < 1 || no < 1 || no > n) return {any};
     std::vector<std::string> out;
     for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {
         char num[8];
         std::snprintf(num, sizeof num, "%05d", i);
         std::string p = any;
         p.replace(at - 5, 5, num);
-        if (!std::ifstream(p, std::ios::binary))
+        if (!std::filesystem::exists(p))
             throw std::runtime_error("missing model shard " + p + " (shard " + std::to_string(i) + " of " +
                                      std::to_string(n) + "; is the download complete?)");
         out.push_back(std::move(p));
     }
     return out;
 }
```

**Verification cases:**
1. Create a temp directory with files `model-00001-of-00002.GGUF` and `model-00002-of-00002.GGUF` (uppercase extension). Call `gguf_split_paths("model-00001-of-00002.GGUF")` and assert it returns both paths in order.
2. Create a directory with only shard 1 of a 3-shard model. Call `gguf_split_paths` on shard 1 and assert it throws with a message naming the missing shard 2 path.

